    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d104">

                <pb facs="0282" n="261" xml:id="pg261"/>

                <head>104. Note From the Director of the National Foreign Assessment Center, Central
                    Intelligence Agency (Bowie) to the
                    President’s Assistant for National Security Affairs (Brzezinski)<anchor n="1" xml:id="d104-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1979-08-07">August 7, 1979</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Zbig:</p>
                <p>In response to your request of 26 July<anchor n="2" xml:id="d104-f2"/> for a
                    thorough evaluation of CIA [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">report number not declassified</hi>]—the report that
                        Qadhafi is planning to announce on 1
                    September the nationalization of US oil company
                    assets in Libya—the attached memorandum has been prepared. Although we tend to
                    believe that Qadhafi is still hoping that
                    the Boeing 747 decision might be reversed again, we cannot rule out
                    nationalization and view it as a credible threat.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d104-f3"
                    /></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#bold">Robert R.
                            Bowie</hi><anchor n="4" xml:id="d104-f4"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d104-a1.xml" xpointer="d104-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d104-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d104-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material,
                    Brzezinski Office File, Country Chron File, Box 29, Libya. Secret; [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">handling restriction not declassified</hi>]. Brzezinski wrote in the upper right-hand
                    corner of the first page: “RP, RH, look into this; what do we need to do? ZB.
                    8/10/79.” The salutation is handwritten.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f2" n="2" xml:id="d104-f2-content">
                <p>In a July 26 memorandum to Tarnoff and
                    Evans, Dodson requested additional
                    information from the Department and the Central Intelligence Agency: “Please
                    provide additional intelligence information bearing on this matter, relevant
                    background on US oil company assets, and current
                    information on Libyan interest in the aircraft.” (Carter Library, National
                    Security Affairs, Brzezinski Material, Brzezinski Office File, Subject Chron
                    File, Box 81, Carter
                    (Billy)/Libya/Hearings: 7–8/80). For the Department of State response, see the
                    Attachment to <ref target="#d105">Document 105</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f3" n="3" xml:id="d104-f3-content">
                <p>Gregg wrote at the bottom of the note: “ZB—This tells you more than you may want
                    to know. Paras 1, 7, 8, 9 &amp; 12 are key. DG. State assessment also
                    attached.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d104-f4" n="4" xml:id="d104-f4-content">
                <p>Bowie signed “Bob” above this typed
                    signature.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
